  "requirement": "The book preprocessor MUST escape requirement names and link targets when inserting badge HTML. It MUST encode badge label and message text in Shields.io URL path components so punctuation cannot change the badge URL structure.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: false.** The implementation looks correct and complete, but the tests leave the central behaviour unchecked.\n\n**Implementation (looks sound)**\n- `shield_path_component` (src/lib.rs:449) encodes every byte except `[A-Za-z0-9.]`.\n  - A space becomes `_`, `_` becomes `__`, and `-` becomes `--`, which are the Shields.io escapes.\n  - Every other byte, including `/ ? # % & \" < >` and UTF-8 bytes, becomes `%XX`. Punctuation therefore cannot change the badge URL's path structure.\n- `shield_badge` (src/lib.rs:433) builds the URL from the encoded label and message. It then HTML-escapes the URL for `src` and escapes the label and message for `alt`.\n- `replace_definitions` (src/lib.rs:278) escapes the full name for the `id` attribute and escapes the detail `href` and its repeated \"See evidence\" link.\n- `replace_references` (src/lib.rs:373) escapes the chapter `href`, which includes the anchor built from the name.\n- `escape_html` (src/lib.rs:775) escapes `& < > \" '`.\n- I found no other place that builds badge HTML with unescaped names or targets.\n  - Other callers of `shield_badge`, such as `render_detail_sections` in src/index.rs, pass through it.\n  - The other `escape_html` uses in commands.rs, fixme.rs and index.rs are outside this requirement's scope.\n\n**Tests (thin for the stated obligation)**\n- `shields_badge_urls_escape_requirement_names` (src/lib.rs:998) covers `_`→`__`, `-`→`--`, the space→`_` case, `&`→`&amp;` in the URL query, and `alt` text.\n- `invalid_names_remain_literal_and_html_is_escaped` (src/lib.rs:983) checks only that a namespace containing `&` yields `alt=\"req a&amp;b.good\"`.\n- Nothing asserts percent-encoding of the characters that could actually alter URL structure (`/`, `?`, `#`, `%`, `&`, quotes, `<`, `>`, non-ASCII). The requirement is specifically about punctuation not changing the URL.\n- Nothing asserts that the `id` and `href` attributes are HTML-escaped when a name or namespace contains special characters. In the `a&b` test, the `id=\"habeas-req-a&amp;b.good\"` and the `%26` in the URL are never checked.\n- The `href` escaping in `replace_references` is also untested for special characters.\n\nThere are no FIXME comments acknowledging these gaps, so the determination is false rather than FIXME. Tests covering punctuation percent-encoding and `id`/`href` escaping would close it.",
